# KiCad-IOS port patch 0045 (KiCad 10.0.1, GPL-3.0)
# Round 19, Job U: symbol chooser preview panes not visible at all.
# Round 18's sash band-clamps (patch 0044) run before the dialog
# reaches its final size, and each has an escape hatch: the panels'
# FinishSetup() falls back to the *saved* dialog size when the
# splitter has no live extent yet (a ghost extent from another
# display-scale era), and DIALOG_SHIM::LoadControlState() applies
# the banked sash verbatim in the same case. Worse, the restore
# order means no validation ever runs at the final size:
# LoadControlState() fires on InitDialog, which wxQt delivers from
# inside wxDialog::Show(), and DIALOG_SHIM::Show() then applies its
# grow-only __geometry restore and resizes the dialog again. The
# generic splitter applies a restored absolute sash verbatim
# (gravity is suppressed while a sash request is pending) and
# SizeWindows() clamps the second pane's size at 0 -- the preview
# pane is not squished, it is exactly 0 px. Saves were never
# validated either, so a collapsed close re-banked sash ~ width-28
# into both stores, renewing the poison every era. On the paint
# side, a preview's first paint is a one-shot ForceRefresh that
# silently no-ops while its canvas is zero-sized or not yet shown,
# and the footprint widget's already-displayed cache suppresses
# any retry for the same footprint.
# This patch: (1) DIALOG_SHIM::Show() gains a final sash
# validation pass at the end of the show path -- the first
# validation that runs with the dialog at its final size -- plus
# save-side clamping in SaveControlState() and a skip (not
# verbatim apply) in LoadControlState() when the splitter has no
# live extent; (2) the three chooser panels' FinishSetup() clamps
# now derive a fallback extent from the parent's post-clamp client
# size and skip the restore when no usable extent exists;
# (3) the symbol and footprint chooser panels gain a layout-heal
# timer (the panels' existing wxTimer idiom; Qt-backed timers fire
# inside the chooser's true-modal loop) that re-validates the
# sashes at the host's settled size, writes the healed values
# back, and re-displays both previews at real canvas sizes,
# bypassing the footprint widget's already-displayed cache.
# Apply with: patch -p1 (from the KiCad source root), after
# patches 0001-0044.
#
